WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Brexit has been in the news
a lot lately,

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.104
and there's still quite a few
people, specifically Americans,

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.105 line:92%
who don't fully understand it.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
Luckily, I saw this commercial
last night that I think

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
explains everything you need
to know about the topic.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.078 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:16.216 line:92%
♪♪ -Happy birthday to you ♪♪

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.751 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thanks, you guys!

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I love
our little get-togethers.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know what
I don't love?

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What?
-Not understanding everything

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's going on
with the world today.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.861 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's so confusing.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, for example,
what is Brexit?

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:34.434
-I'm pretty sure Brexit's the
most important meal of the day.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not quite.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.606
Brexit is just a term for
Britain's recent decision

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.207 line:92%
to leave the European Union.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:41.775 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Tell me more.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, some British people
want to control

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:44.711 line:92%
their own trade agreements

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of having them
controlled

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.914 line:92%
by a larger, unorganized body,

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.650
while other British people think
it's better to be part of

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
a group of bodies
that all work together.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Like an orgy.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I still don't understand
what Brexit is.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:58.591 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's simple.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
The vote for Brexit
was called by David Cameron,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
the former Prime Minister
of the United Kingdom

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.530 line:92%
who never thought it would pass.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then it did,
so he stepped down.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then he was replaced by
Theresa May,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.834 line:92%
who was initially against Brexit

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
but now is in charge of
carrying it out.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The way I'm in charge of
carrying my dog out

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he needs to go
to the bathroom.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:14.674 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He has dementia.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then in November, negotiators
agreed on the framework

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the future relationship
between the E.U. and the U.K.,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is not
a binding legal document

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.818
but more of a commitment
to negotiate in good faith,

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:28.321
which is set out in Article 184
of the withdrawal agreement.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that clears
everything up.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.224 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Oh, no, it doesn't.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So did the U.K.
leave the E.U. or not?

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.662
-Well, the majority of citizens
voted to leave. So, yes.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.531
But then they spent two years
debating how to leave. So, no.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:42.135
But then Theresa May made a new
law saying they have to leave.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:42.502 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, yes!

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then Parliament
rejected her deal.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So who knows?

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do now.
-No, you don't.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure, I do.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.311 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-So are they leaving?

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They're trying.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Imagine a divorce.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A girl can dream.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-While Britain is definitely
leaving the E.U....

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-E-u!
Sorry, I just farted.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They just haven't worked out
the terms.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:04.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
But either way,
they'll exit on March 29th.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.559 line:92%
-March 29th, that's my birthday.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait, if March 29th
is your birthday,

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
then why are we eating
this cake?

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.000 line:92%
-I guess I had a brain Brexit.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:24.344
-America. Be glad we got out of
Britain when we did.

